ARM: dts: n8x0: keep the bootloader's GPIO outputs

NOLO drives GPIO outputs nothing in the kernel claims, the S1D13745's
power-down line (GPIO 15) and the LP5521's among them. The hwmod code
soft-reset the GPIO banks at boot, which turned them all into inputs:
on a real N810 the display controller powered down (it read as revision
0x00, "line buffer not ready", and the screen stayed dark) and the
LP5521 stopped answering (QEMU's models don't care). Nokia's kernel
never reset the GPIO banks: ti,no-reset-on-init for them.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap2420-n8x0-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap2420-n8x0-common.dtsi
@@ -206,3 +206,25 @@
 		powerdown-gpios = <&gpio4 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* gpio 97 */
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Keep the GPIO outputs NOLO drives that no driver claims (the S1D13745's
+ * power-down line, GPIO 15, among them, until its driver takes it). Nokia's
+ * kernel never reset the GPIO banks; a reset at boot turned GPIO 15 into an
+ * input, which powered the display controller down.
+ */
+&gpio1 {
+	ti,no-reset-on-init;
+};
+
+&gpio2 {
+	ti,no-reset-on-init;
+};
+
+&gpio3 {
+	ti,no-reset-on-init;
+};
+
+&gpio4 {
+	ti,no-reset-on-init;
+};
